I'll analyze the method calls in the chat service and compare them with the actual method signatures in the chats store to identify and fix the mismatches.

## Analysis

After reviewing both files, I found several method call mismatches:

| Issue | Location | Current Call | Expected Signature | Fix |
|-------|----------|--------------|-------------------|-----|
| 1 | chat.js line 76 | `updateMessage()` with 3 params | expects `{ chat, message }` | Restructure parameters |
| 2 | chat.js line 86 | `updateMessage()` with 3 params | expects `{ chat, message }` | Restructure parameters |
| 3 | chat.js line 99 | `updateMessages()` params format | expects specific structure | Reformat message updates |
| 4 | chats.js line 245 | `updateMessage()` receives wrong params | method expects `message` object with `doc_id` | Fix in store action |
| 5 | chats.js line 283 | `updateMessage()` batch call format | needs proper message object | Fix message format |

